---
description: Manual tests warn and return when required env is missing.
globs: '**/*.manual.test.ts,**/*.manual.test.tsx'
alwaysApply: false
---

If a manual test needs an environment variable or other caller-supplied
parameter and it is missing, `console.warn` the usage string and `return`.
Do not throw — throwing fails CI or a `TEST_TYPES=manual` run that includes
the file without those parameters.

```typescript
const inputPath = process.env.REDACTION_INPUT_PATH;
if (!inputPath) {
  console.warn(
    'Skipping test. To run, run: REDACTION_INPUT_PATH=file.pdf yarn manual-jest path/to/file.manual.test.ts'
  );
  return;
}
```
